<title>UK: Italy's Prodi not worried by lira fluctuation.</title>
<headline>Italy's Prodi not worried by lira fluctuation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Friday that he was not worried by recent strength in the lira.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters after talks with British Prime Minister John Major, Prodi said the lira's central rate of 990 per German mark in the European exchange rate mechanism had been set just a few weeks ago.</p>
<p>&quot;If the rate of exchange goes a little up from that, it has no real meaning. They are completely normal fluctuations and so I am not worried about that,&quot; Prodi said.</p>
</text>
